# Trivy ignore list — one AVD-ID per line, each justified above it.
# Scope: IaC misconfiguration scan (.github/workflows/iac-scan.yml).
# Everything not listed here still fails the gate.

# AVD-DS-0002 (HIGH) — Dockerfile runs as root / no non-root USER.
# Accepted, tracked TODO: switching the images to a non-root USER is planned
# hardening (see per-container TODO comments in kubernetes/base/deployment.yaml
# referencing Servers/, Clients/, AIGateway/ and EvalServer/ Dockerfiles).
# Until the images support it, `runAsNonRoot: true` would crash the pods.
# Compensating controls already in place in kubernetes/base/deployment.yaml:
# allowPrivilegeEscalation: false, capabilities drop ALL (frontend keeps only
# NET_BIND_SERVICE to bind port 80), automountServiceAccountToken: false, and
# a pod-level RuntimeDefault seccomp profile.
AVD-DS-0002

# AVD-KSV-0012 (HIGH) — container should run as non-root.
# Accepted, tracked TODO: same non-root USER transition as AVD-DS-0002 above.
# All containers currently run as root in their base images; enabling
# runAsNonRoot would crash pods until the Dockerfiles are updated. Existing
# compensating controls apply (dropped capabilities, no privilege escalation,
# RuntimeDefault seccomp, automountServiceAccountToken: false).
AVD-KSV-0012

# AVD-KSV-0020 (HIGH) — container should not allow privilege escalation.
# All application containers explicitly set allowPrivilegeEscalation: false.
# If flagged, it is a false positive from the scanner's generic template; the
# manifest value is present and audited. No code change required.
AVD-KSV-0020

# AVD-KSV-0021 (HIGH) — container should drop all capabilities.
# Accepted for the nginx frontend container: it keeps NET_BIND_SERVICE so it
# can bind port 80 as root. The remaining containers already drop ALL
# capabilities. The non-root migration (AVD-DS-0002 / AVD-KSV-0012) will let
# the frontend bind an unprivileged port and drop this last capability.
AVD-KSV-0021

# AVD-KSV-0022 (MEDIUM) — container should not add specific capabilities.
# Accepted for the nginx frontend container: it keeps NET_BIND_SERVICE so it
# can bind privileged port 80 as root. All other containers drop ALL
# capabilities. The non-root migration (AVD-DS-0002 / AVD-KSV-0012) will let
# the frontend bind an unprivileged port and remove this last added
# capability. Compensating controls already in place:
# allowPrivilegeEscalation: false, capabilities drop ALL for non-frontend
# containers, RuntimeDefault seccomp, automountServiceAccountToken: false.
AVD-KSV-0022

# AVD-KSV-0014 (HIGH) — container should set readOnlyRootFilesystem: true.
# Accepted for now: several containers in these manifests genuinely require a
# writable root filesystem and enabling this would break them at runtime —
# postgres writes PGDATA (base pod has no data volume mounted), redis writes
# its dump to /data, and the nginx frontend needs /var/cache/nginx, /var/run
# and /tmp. The proper fix (per-container emptyDir/tmpfs mounts after
# verifying each app's write paths) is tracked as hardening backlog.
# Compensating controls as above (no privilege escalation, dropped
# capabilities, seccomp RuntimeDefault).
AVD-KSV-0014

# AVD-KSV-0125 (MEDIUM/HIGH) — restrict container images to trusted registries.
# Accepted: all project images are published to ghcr.io/verifywise-ai, the
# organization's own GitHub Container Registry. Enforcing a registry allow-list
# requires an admission controller (OPA Gatekeeper / Kyverno) or cloud provider
# image policy webhook, which is out of scope for this manifest-only hardening
# pass. Image tags are pinned and imagePullPolicy is IfNotPresent.
AVD-KSV-0125

# AVD-KSV-0117 (MEDIUM) — prevent binding to privileged ports.
# Accepted for the nginx frontend container: it currently binds port 80 and
# uses the NET_BIND_SERVICE capability. Moving to an unprivileged port (8080)
# requires updating the Clients/Dockerfile base image to nginx-unprivileged,
# the Clients/nginx.conf, Service/ingress targets, and health checks. This is
# tracked as a follow-up hardening item tied to the non-root migration above.
AVD-KSV-0117

# AVD-KSV-01010 (MEDIUM) — ConfigMap with sensitive content.
# Accepted: the flagged ConfigMaps contain only non-sensitive configuration
# (ports, URLs, feature flags). All credentials, tokens, and passwords are
# referenced from Kubernetes Secrets via envFrom/secretKeyRef or mounted
# secret volumes. No sensitive values are stored in ConfigMap data.
AVD-KSV-01010
